WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.364
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 7: Nature’s Power.

2
00:00:03.444 --> 00:00:04.242
In this unit,

3
00:00:04.322 --> 00:00:11.804
you will explore the incredible and sometimes dangerous
forces of the natural world.You will learn about natural

4
00:00:11.884 --> 00:00:13.627
disasters such as cyclones,

5
00:00:13.707 --> 00:00:15.653
earthquakes, floods, droughts,

6
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:23.621
and volcanic eruptions.You will discover how communities in
East Africa and around the world prepare for these events,

7
00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:27.875
respond when they strike, and
rebuild afterwards.Along the way,

8
00:00:27.955 --> 00:00:33.884
you will build a strong set of vocabulary
words related to planning, science, government,

9
00:00:33.964 --> 00:00:38.544
and community action.You will also
study an important grammar topic —

10
00:00:38.624 --> 00:00:46.646
how to use the Past Simple and Past Continuous tenses together,
joined by connecting words like while, when, and until —

11
00:00:46.726 --> 00:00:50.833
to describe events that happened at the same time in the past.

12
00:00:50.913 --> 00:00:56.505
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

13
00:00:56.585 --> 00:01:04.875
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use and understand
key vocabulary about natural forces, science, planning,

14
00:01:04.955 --> 00:01:06.703
government, and community.

15
00:01:06.783 --> 00:01:13.596
You will also read and discuss a text about natural
disasters and how communities respond to them.

16
00:01:13.676 --> 00:01:21.754
You will also identify the Past Simple tense (for completed
actions) and the Past Continuous tense (for actions that

17
00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:24.919
were happening when something else occurred).

18
00:01:24.999 --> 00:01:27.522
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

19
00:01:27.602 --> 00:01:33.945
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: conduction,
pollination, stratosphere, excavation, mechanisation,

20
00:01:34.025 --> 00:01:34.697
illustration.

21
00:01:34.777 --> 00:01:39.385
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

22
00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:43.030
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

23
00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:48.697
The reading sequence includes When Nature
Speaks and The Speech Under the Baobab, part 1.

24
00:01:48.777 --> 00:01:49.588
Read actively.

25
00:01:49.668 --> 00:01:53.981
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

26
00:01:54.061 --> 00:01:58.120
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

27
00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.228
The first language focus is Past Simple vs Past Continuous.

28
00:02:02.308 --> 00:02:08.146
What it means and why it matters The Past
Simple describes actions that are finished.

29
00:02:08.226 --> 00:02:15.945
The Past Continuous describes actions that were happening
— still in progress — at a certain moment in the past.

30
00:02:16.025 --> 00:02:17.755
When we use them together,

31
00:02:17.835 --> 00:02:24.440
we can tell vivid stories about events that
happened at the same time or interrupted each other.

32
00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:29.523
This is especially useful when
describing natural disasters, emergencies,

33
00:02:29.603 --> 00:02:33.283
or any event where many things were happening at once.

34
00:02:33.363 --> 00:02:40.873
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

35
00:02:40.953 --> 00:02:45.285
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: News Presenter Role-Play.

36
00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:49.633
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

37
00:02:49.713 --> 00:02:52.942
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

38
00:02:53.022 --> 00:02:56.381
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

39
00:02:56.461 --> 00:02:58.028
You are ready to begin.

40
00:02:58.108 --> 00:03:05.116
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

41
00:03:05.196 --> 00:03:08.553
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

42
00:03:08.633 --> 00:03:16.500
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
